// Briarguard

@100 = ~Briarguard~
@101 = ~Briarguard~
@102 = ~BRIARGUARD: Some halflings guard the hedgerows rather than tend them. They wear what the wild gives (hide, chitin, dragon scale), carry a stout club, and fight with the thorns at their back. Fire and frost wash off them like rain off a holly leaf.

Advantages:
– May reach grandmastery in clubs, quarterstaffs, slings and short bows.
– Small and Nimble: +2 AC.
– Heartwood Hide: resistance to fire, cold, electricity and acid: 10% at level 1, 25% at 5, 40% at 10, 60% at 15 and 80% at 20.
– Wild Stride: immune to entangle, web and Spike Growth; from level 12, also to hold, paralysis and slow. Haste and Boots of Speed still work.
– Innate abilities: Entangle and Barkskin from level 1 (Barkskin twice a day from level 9), Strength of the Oak from level 4 (+2 Strength and Constitution for 1 turn; up to three times a day), Iron Skins from level 10 (twice a day from 16), and Wake the Hedge from level 14.
  WAKE THE HEDGE: The hedgerow stands up and fights for 2 turns: a Bramble Man, a Thornwood Guardian from level 18, or a Young Treant from level 22.
– Find Familiar: once a day, calls a badger that grows with the Briarguard and adds to its hit points while it lives.

Disadvantages:
– Natural armour only: leather, hide, Ankheg Plate and dragon scale, but no studded leather or metal armour.
– May only use clubs, quarterstaffs, slings and short bows.
– May only use bucklers and small shields.
– Requires Wisdom 13 or higher.
– Must be a neutral good or true neutral halfling.~

@110 = ~Briarguard~
@111 = ~The Briarguard's heartwood hide and wild stride.~

@120 = ~Entangle~
@121 = ~Barkskin~
@122 = ~Iron Skins~

@125 = ~Strength of the Oak~
@126 = ~Strength of the Oak

For 1 turn, the Briarguard gains +2 Strength and +2 Constitution.~

@130 = ~Wake the Hedge~
@131 = ~Wake the Hedge

The hedgerow stands up and fights beside the Briarguard for 2 turns: a Bramble Man, a Thornwood Guardian from level 18, or a Young Treant from level 22. Its blows entangle what they hit, and like all wood it burns easily. Death Spell cannot kill it.~
@132 = ~Bramble Man~
@133 = ~Thornwood Guardian~
@134 = ~Young Treant~

@140 = ~Briar Patch~
@141 = ~Briar Patch

Thorns burst from the ground: creatures in the area are entangled (save vs breath) and take 2d6 piercing damage each round for 3 rounds. Wild Stride lets the Briarguard fight inside it.~

@145 = ~Call the Pack~
@146 = ~Call the Pack

Summons a cave bear and two dire wolves for 1 turn. Death Spell cannot kill them. While the pack stands, the Briarguard gains +2 to hit and immunity to fear.~
@147 = ~Pack Bear~
@148 = ~Pack Wolf~

@150 = ~Heartwood~
@151 = ~Heartwood

Each time this ability is chosen, the Briarguard gains 5% resistance to slashing, piercing, crushing and missile damage.~

@155 = ~Deep Roots~
@156 = ~Deep Roots

Strength of the Oak also regenerates 3 hit points per round while it lasts.~

@160 = ~Ironwood~
@161 = ~Ironwood

The Briarguard's weapons count as +3 weapons for what they can hit, or +4 with a second pick.~

@165 = ~Badger's Fury~
@166 = ~Badger's Fury

For 1 turn, the Briarguard gains +1 attack per round, +2 damage, and immunity to charm and confusion. Its badger nearby rages too, gaining +1 attack per round and +2 damage.~

@170 = ~Thornhide~
@171 = ~Thornhide

For 3 turns, anything that hits the Briarguard takes 2d6 piercing damage.~

@175 = ~Hedge Shelter~
@176 = ~Hedge Shelter

For 1 turn, the Briarguard and its allies nearby gain +3 AC and 25% resistance to fire, cold, electricity and acid.~

@190 = ~Hedgerow Badger~
@191 = ~Sett Badger~
@192 = ~Grey Brock~
@193 = ~Old Brock~
@194 = ~Elder of the Sett~
@195 = ~Find Familiar~
@196 = ~Find Familiar

Once a day, the Briarguard calls its badger, which fights beside it for one day. The badger grows with the Briarguard: a Hedgerow Badger, then a Sett Badger from level 7, a Grey Brock from 12, an Old Brock from 18 and the Elder of the Sett from 24. While the badger lives, the Briarguard gains extra hit points: 8, rising to 45 for the Elder.~
@197 = ~The badger falls, and the Briarguard feels the loss.~

@180 = ~Briarguards cannot use this item.~
